NAME: maturity-neuvector
LAST DEPLOYED: Wed Nov 11 02:11:40 2026
NAMESPACE: maturity-neuvector
STATUS: deployed
REVISION: 1
TEST SUITE: None
NOTES:
Get the NeuVector URL by running these commands:
  CLUSTER_IP=$(kubectl get --namespace maturity-neuvector -o jsonpath="{.spec.clusterIP}" services neuvector-service-webui)
  TARGET_PORT=$(kubectl get --namespace maturity-neuvector -o jsonpath="{.spec.ports[0].targetPort}" services neuvector-service-webui)
  echo https://$CLUSTER_IP:$TARGET_PORT

NOTE: Use below command to get the password to login to NeuVector WebUi using admin account if it is a fresh install and not a restore from PVC, no admin password is set in the configmap or secret. The password is randomly generated during the deployment if AWS cloud billing is enabled.

To get the bootstrap password:

kubectl get secret --namespace maturity-neuvector neuvector-bootstrap-secret -o go-template='{{.data.bootstrapPassword|base64decode}}{{ "\n" }}'
